```java
try {
    repository.save(order);
} catch (SQLException e) {
    // BAD: original cause discarded; you only see the vague wrapper
    throw new ServiceException("checkout failed");
}
// Trace shows ServiceException with NO 'Caused by' -> root cause is gone.
```

```java
try {
    repository.save(order);
} catch (SQLException e) {
    // GOOD: pass the cause so the chain (and root) survives
    throw new ServiceException("checkout failed", e);
}
// Trace now shows:
//   ServiceException: checkout failed
//   Caused by: SQLException: connection refused  <-- the real origin
```

Always pass the caught exception as the cause; otherwise you keep the symptom and throw away the diagnosis.

