```java
public int nameLength(Map<String,String> users, String id) {
    String name = users.get(id);
    if (name == null) return 0;            // explicit guard
    return name.length();
}
// Or, expressing 'maybe absent' in the type:
return Optional.ofNullable(users.get(id)).map(String::length).orElse(0);
```

The trace tells you *where*; the fix is deciding what should happen when the value is legitimately absent.

