// No base case: factorial recurses forever
int factorial(int n) {
    return n * factorial(n - 1); // never stops; overflows the stack
}
// Trace repeats endlessly:
//   at com.app.MathUtil.factorial(MathUtil.java:5)
//   at com.app.MathUtil.factorial(MathUtil.java:5)   ... x thousands
```

```java
long factorial(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 1;          // base case: recursion terminates
    return n * factorial(n - 1);
}

// For deep inputs, iteration avoids the stack entirely:
long factorialIter(int n) {
    long result = 1;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) result *= i;
    return result;
}
```

The repeating method in the trace tells you which recursion is unbounded; fix the base case or convert to a loop.

