```java
try {
    repo.save(order);
} catch (SQLException e) {
    throw new ServiceException("checkout failed", e); // GOOD: cause kept
}
// Trace: ServiceException ... Caused by: SQLException: connection refused
```

You can also wrap a checked exception in an unchecked one this way to avoid polluting signatures, while still keeping the diagnosis.
